# builder/Containerfile is built with the three binaries in its context, which
# its own header tells you to compile there:
#
#   for r in zpkb zpkm zpkx; do go build -o builder/$r github.com/go-zpkg/$r/...
#
# They were COMMITTED instead — 29 MB of stripped, aarch64-only executables in
# a repository whose own pre-push gate now refuses that class (#442). Named one
# per line rather than as a glob: a pattern that happens to match a source file
# later is how a rename leaves a binary behind in the first place.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND THE RETIRED NAMES ARE LISTED TOO, BECAUSE THEY ARE THE ONES THAT WERE
# ACTUALLY THERE. This list arrived in #449 carrying only the CURRENT spellings
# — zbk, zpkgm, zpkgx — while the committed files were `bk`, `pkgm` and `pkgx`
# from before the rename. So it ignored three files that did not exist and left
# the three that did, untracked by nobody and committed by everybody; #449's
# own body said they were "gone from HEAD" and they were not. An ignore rule
# written from the name a thing SHOULD have cannot see the name it HAS.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND IT HAPPENED AGAIN, ONE GENERATION LATER — found 2026-11-15 while
# sweeping `bk` out of this repository. The list held `zpkgm` and `zpkgx`,
# which are a spelling nothing has used since the modules became
# `github.com/go-zpkg/zpkm` and `.../zpkx`; the loop above said `zpkgm zpkgx`
# too, while builder/Containerfile's own loop says `zpkb zpkm zpkx`. So the two
# binaries a reader following the header would actually produce, `zpkm` and
# `zpkx`, were ignored by NOTHING. The CURRENT names are checked against the
# module paths the workflows install, not against memory.
/builder/bk
/builder/pkgm
/builder/pkgx
/builder/zbk
/builder/zpkb
/builder/zpkm
/builder/zpkx
/builder/zpkgm
/builder/zpkgx

# A session waiting on CI writes `prwait -repo O/R N > .prwait-N.log` in the
# checkout, and one of those reached a commit in this repository on 2026-11-18.
# A log that names a pull request is a transient of one turn; nothing here reads
# it, and `git add -A` picks it up by construction.
/.prwait-*.log
